{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UXAoR928ZVYC9h6nzKq3Zn","type":"tool_result","content":"476\t/// Stream/event callback installed on a QUIC context or connection.\n477\t/// Folds the C `void* callback_ctx` into the trait implementor's\n478\t/// state; `stream_ctx` is per-stream and remains a raw pointer\n479\t/// because it is produced and consumed by the application without\n480\t/// the stack interpreting it.\n481\t///\n482\t/// Returns the C `int` directly: `0` for success, or one of the\n483\t/// `_*` codes (e.g. `STREAM_RECEIVE_COMPLETE`) for\n484\t/// special signalling.  Phase 3 may refine to `Result` once the\n485\t/// crate-level error type lands.\n486\t///\n487\t/// `bytes` is `&[u8]` rather than `*const u8 + size_t`; events that\n488\t/// carry no payload pass `&[]`.\n489\tpub trait StreamDataCallback {\n490\t    fn callback(\n491\t        &mut self,\n492\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n493\t        stream_id: u64,\n494\t        bytes: &[u8],\n495\t        fin_or_event: CallbackEvent,\n496\t        stream_ctx: Option<&mut dyn core::any::Any>,\n497\t    ) -> i32;\n498\t}\n499\t\n500\t/// ALPN-selection callback.  Returns the index of the chosen ALPN\n501\t/// in `list`, or any value `>= list.len()` to signal \"none of the\n502\t/// proposed ALPNs is supported\".  C: `AlpnSelect` (the C `_v2`\n503\t/// flavour is folded in — it only differed in the iovec type, which\n504\t/// is now just `&[u8]`).\n505\t/// Application hook the TLS backend invokes to choose one of the\n506\t/// client's proposed ALPN values.  Returns the chosen index into\n507\t/// `list`, or `None` to reject the handshake.\n508\t///\n509\t/// `list` carries the raw bytes off the wire; mapping to the\n510\t/// strongly-typed [`Alpn`] enum is up to the implementor (most\n511\t/// applications keep a small whitelist by string identifier).\n512\tpub trait AlpnSelect {\n513\t    fn select(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic, list: &[&[u8]]) -> Option<usize>;\n514\t}\n515\t\n516\t/// Callback that produces a server-environment-compatible CID.\n517\t/// Folds the C `void* connection_id_cb_data` into the implementor's state.\n518\t/// C: `ConnectionIdCallback`.\n519\tpub trait ConnectionIdCallback {\n520\t    fn produce(\n521\t        &mut self,\n522\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n523\t        connection_id_local: ConnectionId,\n524\t        connection_id_remote: ConnectionId,\n525\t    ) -> ConnectionId;\n526\t}\n527\t\n528\t/// Packet-fuzzer callback.  Folds the C `void* fuzz_ctx` into the\n529\t/// implementor.  Returns the new packet length (which may equal\n530\t/// the input).  C: `Fuzz`.\n531\tpub trait Fuzz {\n532\t    fn fuzz(\n533\t        &mut self,\n534\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n535\t        bytes: &mut [u8],\n536\t        length: usize,\n537\t        header_length: usize,\n538\t    ) -> u32;\n539\t}\n540\t\n541\t/// Direct-receive callback for streams marked with\n542\t/// `mark_direct_receive_stream`.  C:\n543\t/// `StreamDirectReceive`.  Folds `direct_receive_ctx`\n544\t/// into the implementor.\n545\tpub trait StreamDirectReceive {\n546\t    fn receive(\n547\t        &mut self,\n548\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n549\t        stream_id: u64,\n550\t        fin: bool,\n551\t        bytes: &[u8],\n552\t        offset: u64,\n553\t    ) -> i32;\n554\t}\n555\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"513641af-66d9-4e8b-98cd-e59b8e6a1fb7","uuid":"801b9d51-e69c-4da1-bc78-5c722f965b15","timestamp":"2026-05-04T22:23:20.101Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lib.rs","content":"/// Stream/event callback installed on a QUIC context or connection.\n/// Folds the C `void* callback_ctx` into the trait implementor's\n/// state; `stream_ctx` is per-stream and remains a raw pointer\n/// because it is produced and consumed by the application without\n/// the stack interpreting it.\n///\n/// Returns the C `int` directly: `0` for success, or one of the\n/// `_*` codes (e.g. `STREAM_RECEIVE_COMPLETE`) for\n/// special signalling.  Phase 3 may refine to `Result` once the\n/// crate-level error type lands.\n///\n/// `bytes` is `&[u8]` rather than `*const u8 + size_t`; events that\n/// carry no payload pass `&[]`.\npub trait StreamDataCallback {\n    fn callback(\n        &mut self,\n        connection: &mut Connection,\n        stream_id: u64,\n        bytes: &[u8],\n        fin_or_event: CallbackEvent,\n        stream_ctx: Option<&mut dyn core::any::Any>,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n\n/// ALPN-selection callback.  Returns the index of the chosen ALPN\n/// in `list`, or any value `>= list.len()` to signal \"none of the\n/// proposed ALPNs is supported\".  C: `AlpnSelect` (the C `_v2`\n/// flavour is folded in — it only differed in the iovec type, which\n/// is now just `&[u8]`).\n/// Application hook the TLS backend invokes to choose one of the\n/// client's proposed ALPN values.  Returns the chosen index into\n/// `list`, or `None` to reject the handshake.\n///\n/// `list` carries the raw bytes off the wire; mapping to the\n/// strongly-typed [`Alpn`] enum is up to the implementor (most\n/// applications keep a small whitelist by string identifier).\npub trait AlpnSelect {\n    fn select(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic, list: &[&[u8]]) -> Option<usize>;\n}\n\n/// Callback that produces a server-environment-compatible CID.\n/// Folds the C `void* connection_id_cb_data` into the implementor's state.\n/// C: `ConnectionIdCallback`.\npub trait ConnectionIdCallback {\n    fn produce(\n        &mut self,\n        quic: &mut Quic,\n        connection_id_local: ConnectionId,\n        connection_id_remote: ConnectionId,\n    ) -> ConnectionId;\n}\n\n/// Packet-fuzzer callback.  Folds the C `void* fuzz_ctx` into the\n/// implementor.  Returns the new packet length (which may equal\n/// the input).  C: `Fuzz`.\npub trait Fuzz {\n    fn fuzz(\n        &mut self,\n        connection: &mut Connection,\n        bytes: &mut [u8],\n        length: usize,\n        header_length: usize,\n    ) -> u32;\n}\n\n/// Direct-receive callback for streams marked with\n/// `mark_direct_receive_stream`.  C:\n/// `StreamDirectReceive`.  Folds `direct_receive_ctx`\n/// into the implementor.\npub trait StreamDirectReceive {\n    fn receive(\n        &mut self,\n        connection: &mut Connection,\n        stream_id: u64,\n        fin: bool,\n        bytes: &[u8],\n        offset: u64,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n","numLines":80,"startLine":476,"totalLines":2425}}}
